  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present design has critical inherent risk from untrusted public issue content reaching shell execution, self-configuration, and broad GitHub egress under A4 autonomy. Residual remains high because the only declared preventive control on those paths is prompt-based and dependent; the container does not constrain the sink. Forecast is critical, driven most by decay of ctrl.prompt_rules under model_upgrade/longer_task_horizon and by the planned new_mcp_server trigger for Slack, which would add a new S3 egress path. Manual validation only; scripts were not available in this environment."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration in prompt.md, .agent/config.yaml, and runtime notes, not observed runtime behavior.",
    "No source code, tool schemas, IaC, or runtime telemetry were provided, so confidence is lower for implementation details such as actual shell sandboxing, secret mounting, and audit logging.",
    "The planned Slack MCP server is assessed only as a forecast because no server configuration, tool manifest, or agent card was supplied.",
    "Repository file contents are treated as untrusted because public contributors can influence code in public repositories, but the exact repository contribution model was not described."
  ]
}
